TEXT -448 -176 Left 2 ;Experiment 6(c): 2:1 Multiplexer using CMOS Transmission Gates
TEXT -448 -128 Left 1 ;Y = (S' . D0) + (S . D1)    TG0 passes D0 when S=0,  TG1 passes D1 when S=1
TEXT -448 1024 Left 2 !.tran 0 40m 0 10u
TEXT -448 1072 Left 1 ;Inverter MP1/MN1 makes Sbar. TG = NMOS || PMOS with complementary gates; NMOS body -> GND, PMOS body -> VDD.
TEXT -448 1104 Left 1 ;Plot V(s), V(d0), V(d1), V(y). Each 5 ms slot is one row of the truth table (S D0 D1 = 000 ... 111).
TEXT -432 240 Right 2 ;VIEW SELECT S -->
TEXT -432 464 Right 2 ;VIEW INPUT D0 -->
TEXT -432 688 Right 2 ;VIEW INPUT D1 -->
TEXT 544 448 Right 2 ;VIEW OUTPUT Y -->
TEXT -448 1168 Left 1 ;HOW TO VIEW WAVEFORMS  (note only - you may delete it, the circuit is not affected)\n1. Click Run (running-man icon). A black waveform window opens; it is empty at first.\n2. In this schematic, put the mouse on a wire marked VIEW. The cursor becomes a red probe. Click.\n3. That voltage is drawn in the waveform window, with its name, e.g. V(out), in the same colour above it.\n4. Click the other VIEW wires to add more signals. All share one time axis (read left to right).\n5. One signal per pane: click the waveform window, Plot Settings > Add Plot Pane, click the new pane, then click the next wire.\n6. Remove a trace: Plot Settings > Delete Traces, then click the trace name. Press Esc to stop deleting.\nSignals:  SELECT S = V(s)   |   DATA D0 = V(d0)   |   DATA D1 = V(d1)   |   OUTPUT Y = V(y)
